# Build context allowlist for deploy/Dockerfile (BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore next to the Dockerfile).
# Everything is excluded unless listed, so .env files, data/, .venv/, mlruns/, eval/ and app/ never reach the
# builder, even when the image is built from a working copy instead of a release tarball. The demo bundle is the one
# organizer-derived input allowed in; the build checks it against the committed lock before using it.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!agent/
!api/
!ml/
!data_engineering/
!deploy/serve.py
!deploy/lock.py
!deploy/demo-bundle.lock.json
!deploy/demo-bundle/
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.env
**/.env.*
